<!--
  labwc session config for the Smart First Aid Box cabinet kiosk.

  STATUS: NEVER APPLIED. This has not been parsed by labwc on hardware. Element names
  were written from the labwc config documentation, not read off the device. Confirm
  every element marked VERIFY against `man 5 labwc-config` for the labwc version the Pi
  actually runs (ask labwc for its version), and watch the user journal for XML parse
  errors after the first reconfigure — labwc reports them there rather than refusing to
  start.

  ============================================================================
  !! STOP. DO NOT COPY THIS FILE OVER AN EXISTING rc.xml. !!

  /home/technology/.config/labwc/rc.xml on this Pi already holds work that this file
  does not reproduce and must not destroy:

    · a measured five-point touch calibrationMatrix for the ADS7846 panel
    · a <touch> mapping whose mapToOutput was repaired to HDMI-A-1 (it had been
      pointing at NOOP-1, which is why touch appeared dead)
    · mouseEmulation=yes on that touch device

  Those numbers are NOT written into this template, deliberately: inventing calibration
  coefficients would be worse than having none, because wrong ones look like they work.
  The measured set lives outside this repo at
  ~/Desktop/Codex/pi5-tailscale-setup/touch-calibration-measured.json (confirmed present
  while writing this) and, on the device, inside the current rc.xml and its backups.

  Procedure:
    1. Back up the live file first (see ../README.md, step 0).
    2. Open the backup, copy the <touch .../> element and the <libinput> device entry
       carrying calibrationMatrix, VERBATIM.
    3. Paste them into the marked slot below.
    4. Only then install this file.
  ============================================================================
-->
<labwc_config>

  <core>
    <!-- No gap between windows and no edge snapping to fight the fullscreen browser. -->
    <gap>0</gap>
  </core>

  <theme>
    <!-- Nothing should be visible around the browser. Chromium in kiosk mode is
         fullscreen and undecorated already; this is the compositor-side belt. -->
    <cornerRadius>0</cornerRadius>
  </theme>

  <!--
    KEYBINDINGS — the removal mechanism.

    labwc installs its stock keybindings (window switching, close window, terminal,
    workspace switching, the window menu) when <keyboard> contains <default />.
    This block contains NO <default /> and NO <keybind> entries, so the session starts
    with an empty keymap. That is the removal: there is nothing to "unbind" one by one.

    Removed by consequence, all of them defaults in a normal labwc session:
      · A-F4          close window
      · W-Return / A-F2 style terminal or run-command launchers
      · A-Tab         window switcher
      · W-Left/Right, A-C-Left/Right, W-1..4   workspace switching
      · W-Down / iconify bindings   minimise
      · A-space       client (window) menu

    VERIFY: that an EMPTY <keyboard> means "no keybinds" rather than "fall back to
    defaults" on the installed labwc version. This is the single most important thing
    to test in the escape-key sweep in ../README.md, because if the fallback behaviour
    is the opposite of what is assumed here, every one of the bindings above is still
    live and the kiosk is not locked at all. Test it with a keyboard plugged in, not by
    reading this comment.
  -->
  <keyboard>
  </keyboard>

  <!--
    MOUSE / TOUCH CONTEXT BINDINGS — same mechanism, no <default />.
    Suppresses the root-window menu on click and the titlebar context actions.
    With mouseEmulation on the touch panel, a long press or a stray two-finger contact
    would otherwise be able to raise the root menu. menu.xml is emptied as well, so
    this is defence in depth rather than the only barrier.
  -->
  <mouse>
  </mouse>

  <windowRules>
    <!--
      VERIFY the attribute names and the identifier matching for this labwc version;
      windowRule syntax has changed across releases. If labwc logs a parse error here,
      delete this whole <windowRules> block first — it is a nicety. Chromium started
      in kiosk mode is already fullscreen and undecorated without it.
    -->
    <windowRule identifier="chromium*" serverDecoration="no" skipTaskbar="yes" skipWindowSwitcher="yes" />
  </windowRules>

  <!--
    ========================================================================
    PASTE THE TOUCHSCREEN CONFIGURATION FROM YOUR BACKED-UP rc.xml HERE.

    Two things to transplant, both copied verbatim from the backup:
      1. the <libinput> block containing the ADS7846 device entry and its
         <calibrationMatrix> (the measured five-point fit)
      2. the <touch ... mapToOutput="HDMI-A-1" mouseEmulation="yes" /> element

    No numbers are supplied here on purpose. If this slot is still empty when you
    install the file, touch will be uncalibrated or mapped to the wrong output, and the
    failure mode is taps landing in the wrong place rather than an obvious error.

    After installing, re-check alignment at all four corners AND the centre before
    declaring it working — a matrix can be right at the corners and wrong in the middle.
    ========================================================================
  -->

</labwc_config>
